<item><title>Togo land forum puts community rights and investment on agenda</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-land-forum-puts-community-rights-and-investment-on-da0b7e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-land-forum-puts-community-rights-and-investment-on-da0b7e/</guid><category>Togo</category><description>Representatives met in Kara from 18 to 20 November to discuss land conflicts, community protections and access to land.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:40:54 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" length="29610" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Togo buries Father Vivien Dakloumegan in Agoè-Nyivé</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-buries-father-vivien-dakloumegan-in-agoe-nyive-a790dc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-buries-father-vivien-dakloumegan-in-agoe-nyive-a790dc/</guid><category>Togo</category><description>The Lomé archdiocese priest, who died aged 51 on 19 October, was buried at the cemetery for priests of Petit Séminaire Saint Pie X.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:46:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" length="29610" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Togo arranges return of citizens expelled from Guinea</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-arranges-return-of-citizens-expelled-from-guinea-2965ee/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-arranges-return-of-citizens-expelled-from-guinea-2965ee/</guid><category>Togo</category><description>Lomé is working with Burkina Faso and Mali and with its diplomatic and consular missions to bring home citizens held in reception centres after anti-illegal-mining operations.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:42:46 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-arranges-return-of-citizens-expelled-from-guinea-2965ee/share.jpg" length="38351" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/togo-arranges-return-of-citizens-expelled-from-guinea-2965ee/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Afolabi schedules Togo repentance day for 22 November</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/afolabi-schedules-togo-repentance-day-for-22-november-674f8e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tg/afolabi-schedules-togo-repentance-day-for-22-november-674f8e/</guid><category>Togo</category><description>The nationwide event calls on Togolese to seek forgiveness and pray for peace, with its closing gathering at the Centre for Sports and Recreation (CERFER) grounds in Lomé.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:24:24 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" length="29610" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
